+You will observe that the cache is hit on the second call, demonstrating the effect of the custom cache key logic.
+
+## Inspect cache usage
+
+`dspy.cache.stats()` returns a new dictionary containing `hits`, `mem_hits`,
+`disk_hits`, and `misses`. Each read contributes exactly one result; writes and
+disk-to-memory promotion do not add reads. `dspy.cache.reset_stats()` resets the
+counters without removing cached entries.
+
+Inside `dspy.settings.context(track_usage=True)`, each synchronous or asynchronous
+module result also receives an independent per-call snapshot through
+`Prediction.get_cache_usage()`. Nested module calls are inclusive in the enclosing
+snapshot, while concurrent calls remain isolated. When usage tracking is disabled,
+new predictions have no cache-usage snapshot.
